<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Gregory IX</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1241</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Ugolino di Conti</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gregory IX was pope from 1227 to 1241, a relative of Innocent III. He repeatedly excommunicated Emperor Frederick II and fought him for control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, and from 1231 he appointed papal inquisitors to pursue heresy. He canonised Francis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assisi">Assisi</a> and Dominic, and in 1234 issued the Decretals, a major collection of canon law.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-ix.jpg" alt="Pope Gregory IX" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francesco Bini · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ritratto_di_gregorio_ix,_dalla_facciata_dell%27antica_basilica_di_s._pietro,_1225-50_ca._(museo_di_roma)_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
